/-!
# A very ample invertible module on a proper curve is generated by its global sections

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] — a field `k` and a proper one-dimensional `k`-scheme `X` with
`H⁰(X, 𝒪_X) = k` — let `ℒ` be a very ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module and let `k` be algebraically
closed. This file proves that `ℒ` is generated by its global sections, and records the two
consequences that the vanishing results for curves consume when `deg(ℒ) ≥ 2`: the vanishing
`H⁰(X, ℒ^{⊗ -1}) = 0` and [Stacks, Tag 0B62] at the canonical dualizing sheaf.

## Main results

The elided prefix is `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation`.

* `exists_isClosed_singleton_ne`: **`X` has at least two distinct closed points.**
* `exists_mem_nonvanishingLocus`: **every point of `X` lies in the nonvanishing locus of some
  global section of `ℒ`.**
* `nonempty_generatingSections_of_isRelativelyVeryAmple`: **`ℒ` is generated by its global
  sections.**
* `not_isTrivial_of_two_le_invertibleCurveDegree`: an invertible module of degree at least two is
  not isomorphic to `𝒪_X`.
* `subsingleton_globalSections_tensorPowerModule_neg_one`: `H⁰(X, ℒ^{⊗ -1}) = 0` for a very ample
  `ℒ` of degree at least two.
* `isZero_cohomologyOverField_one_dualizing_tensorSheaf`: `H¹(X, ω_X ⊗ ℒ) = 0` for such an `ℒ`,
  which is [Stacks, Tag 0B62] with its two hypotheses discharged.

## Implementation notes

**Two closed points.** `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isClosed_singleton_ne` produces a closed point
distinct from a given one on any scheme whose space is Jacobson and not a subsingleton. The space
of `X` is Jacobson because `f` is locally of finite type over a field
(`AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType.jacobsonSpace`), and it is not a subsingleton because a
subsingleton space is discrete, hence of topological Krull dimension at most zero, against
`topologicalKrullDim X = 1`.

**Nonvanishing at an arbitrary point.** [Stacks, Tag 0B58] produces a global section of `ℒ`
vanishing at a prescribed closed point and at none of finitely many other prescribed points; here
it is applied at a closed point `x` distinct from a closed point `w` in the closure of the given
point `y`, with `w` as the single avoided point. The nonvanishing locus is open
([Stacks, Tag 01CY]) and contains `w`, and `w ∈ closure {y}` makes every open neighbourhood of `w`
meet `{y}`, so `y` lies in it too. The closed point `w` of `closure {y}` comes from
`Stacks.SerreAffinenessCriterion.exists_isClosed_singleton_mem`, the statement that a nonempty
closed subset of a quasi-compact scheme contains a point closed in the ambient space; `X` is
quasi-compact because `f` is proper.

**Global generation.** Generation by the family of *all* global sections is, by
[Stacks, Tag 01AN] in the span form `AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates`, the
statement that the germs of the global sections span every stalk, and for an invertible module a
single section nonvanishing at a point already spans the stalk there
(`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.span_eq_top_of_mem_nonvanishingLocus`). So the index type of the
generating family is `Γ(ℒ, ⊤)` itself. Unlike
`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isFinGen_of_nonvanishingCover`, no finiteness of the index type is
claimed, so no quasi-compactness is spent.

**The two consequences.** `H⁰(X, ℒ^{⊗ -1}) = 0` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.subsingleton_globalSections_inverse` and
`H¹(X, ω_X ⊗ ℒ) = 0` is
`CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.isZero_firstCohomology_dualizingSheafOverField_tensor`, both of
which take a `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` for `ℒ` and the failure of `ℒ` to be isomorphic
to `𝒪_X`; the first is proved here from very ampleness and the second follows from
`deg(ℒ) ≥ 2`, the degree of a module isomorphic to `𝒪_X` being zero
(`AlgebraicGeometry.invertibleCurveDegree_eq_zero_of_iso_unit`).

**Nothing is carried.** Every hypothesis beyond the situation itself — algebraic closedness of
`k`, very ampleness of `ℒ` and the lower bound on its degree — appears in the statements.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B58](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B58)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B62](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B62)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.Ample (nonvanishingLocus)
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible (tensorPowerModule)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace CohenMacaulayCurveSituation

variable (S : CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.{u})

/-! ### Two closed points -/

/-- **The curve of Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] is not a one-point space.** A subsingleton space
is discrete, hence of topological Krull dimension at most zero, while `X` has dimension one. -/
public theorem not_subsingleton : ¬ Subsingleton S.X := by
  intro hsub
  have := hsub
  have : DiscreteTopology S.X := discreteTopology_iff_forall_isOpen.mpr fun s => by
    rcases s.eq_empty_or_nonempty with rfl | ⟨a, ha⟩
    · exact isOpen_empty
    · rw [show s = Set.univ from
        Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun b => by rw [Subsingleton.elim b a]; exact ha]
      exact isOpen_univ
  have h0 := topologicalKrullDim_zero_of_discreteTopology ↥S.X
  rw [S.dimension_one] at h0
  exact absurd h0 (by decide)

/-- **The curve of Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] has a closed point other than any given one.**
Its space is Jacobson, being locally of finite type over a field, so the closed points are dense;
were they all equal to `y` the space would be a single point, which `not_subsingleton`
excludes. -/
public theorem exists_isClosed_singleton_ne (y : S.X) (hy : IsClosed ({y} : Set S.X)) :
    ∃ x : S.X, IsClosed ({x} : Set S.X) ∧ x ≠ y :=
  have : JacobsonSpace S.X := LocallyOfFiniteType.jacobsonSpace S.f
  AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isClosed_singleton_ne S.not_subsingleton y hy

/-! ### Nonvanishing of a global section at an arbitrary point -/

/-- **Every point of `X` lies in the nonvanishing locus of some global section of a very ample
invertible module `ℒ`**, the base field being algebraically closed.

Pick a closed point `w` in the closure of `y` and, by `exists_isClosed_singleton_ne`, a closed
point `x ≠ w`. [Stacks, Tag 0B58] — in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_globalSection_vanishing_at_isClosed` — gives a global section of `ℒ`
vanishing at `x` but not at `w`. Its nonvanishing locus is open ([Stacks, Tag 01CY]) and contains
`w`, so it meets `{y}`, that is, it contains `y`. -/
public theorem exists_mem_nonvanishingLocus [IsAlgClosed S.k] (L : S.X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    (hL : Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.IsRelativelyVeryAmple S.f L) (y : S.X) :
    ∃ s : Γ(L, ⊤), y ∈ nonvanishingLocus L s := by
  have : CompactSpace S.X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace S.f
  obtain ⟨w, hwy, hwcl⟩ := Stacks.SerreAffinenessCriterion.exists_isClosed_singleton_mem
    (isClosed_closure (s := ({y} : Set S.X))) ⟨y, subset_closure rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨x, hxcl, hxw⟩ := S.exists_isClosed_singleton_ne w hwcl
  obtain ⟨s, -, hs⟩ := exists_globalSection_vanishing_at_isClosed S.f L hL x hxcl
    (fun _ : Unit => w) fun _ => hxw
  refine ⟨s, ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨z, hzs, hzy⟩ := mem_closure_iff.mp hwy _
    (Stacks.NonvanishingOpen.isOpen_nonvanishingLocus S.X L s) (hs ())
  exact Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp hzy ▸ hzs

/-! ### Global generation -/

/-- **A very ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module on the curve of Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] over an
algebraically closed field is generated by its global sections.**

The generating family is the family of *all* global sections of `ℒ`. By [Stacks, Tag 01AN], in
the span form `AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates`, it generates `ℒ` as soon as
its germs span every stalk, and a single global section nonvanishing at a point already spans the
stalk of an invertible module there
(`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.span_eq_top_of_mem_nonvanishingLocus`). Such a section exists at every
point by `exists_mem_nonvanishingLocus`. -/
public theorem nonempty_generatingSections_of_isRelativelyVeryAmple [IsAlgClosed S.k]
    (L : S.X.Modules) [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    (hL : Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.IsRelativelyVeryAmple S.f L) :
    Nonempty L.GeneratingSections := by
  refine ⟨⟨Γ(L, ⊤), fun t => (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.sectionsEquiv S.X L).symm t, ?_⟩⟩
  refine (AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates S.X.ringCatSheaf L _).mpr fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := S.exists_mem_nonvanishingLocus L hL x
  have hval : ∀ t : Γ(L, ⊤),
      ((Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.sectionsEquiv S.X L).symm t).eval (op ⊤) = t :=
    fun t => (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.sectionsEquiv S.X L).apply_symm_apply t
  simp only [hval]
  exact Stacks.FinGenFromCover.span_eq_top_of_mem_nonvanishingLocus L
    (fun t : Γ(L, ⊤) => t) hs

/-! ### The consequences at degree at least two -/

/-- **An invertible `𝒪_X`-module of degree at least two is not isomorphic to `𝒪_X`.** The degree
of a module isomorphic to the structure sheaf is zero
(`AlgebraicGeometry.invertibleCurveDegree_eq_zero_of_iso_unit`). -/
public theorem not_isTrivial_of_two_le_invertibleCurveDegree (L : S.X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    (hd : 2 ≤ invertibleCurveDegree S.k S.f (le_of_eq S.dimension_one) L) :
    ¬ SheafOfModules.IsTrivial S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.property L := by
  rintro ⟨e⟩
  have e' : L ≅ SheafOfModules.unit S.X.ringCatSheaf := e
  rw [invertibleCurveDegree_eq_zero_of_iso_unit S.k S.f (le_of_eq S.dimension_one) L e'] at hd
  omega

/-- **`H⁰(X, ℒ^{⊗ -1}) = 0`** for a very ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module `ℒ` of degree at least two
on the curve of Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] over an algebraically closed field. -/
public theorem subsingleton_globalSections_tensorPowerModule_neg_one [IsAlgClosed S.k]
    (L : S.X.Modules) [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    (hL : Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.IsRelativelyVeryAmple S.f L)
    (hd : 2 ≤ invertibleCurveDegree S.k S.f (le_of_eq S.dimension_one) L) :
    Subsingleton Γ(tensorPowerModule L (-1), ⊤) :=
  subsingleton_globalSections_inverse_of_generatingSections L
    (S.nonempty_generatingSections_of_isRelativelyVeryAmple L hL).some
    (S.not_isTrivial_of_two_le_invertibleCurveDegree L hd)

/-- **`H¹(X, ω_X ⊗ ℒ) = 0`** for a very ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module `ℒ` of degree at least two
on the curve of Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] over an algebraically closed field, where
`ω_X = H^{-1}(f^×(𝒪_{Spec k}))` is the dualizing sheaf of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2]. -/
public theorem isZero_cohomologyOverField_one_dualizing_tensorSheaf [IsAlgClosed S.k]
    (L : S.X.Modules) [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    (hL : Stacks.Tag01VMVeryAmple.IsRelativelyVeryAmple S.f L)
    (hd : 2 ≤ invertibleCurveDegree S.k S.f (le_of_eq S.dimension_one) L) :
    IsZero (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f
      ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨S.X.presheaf,
        Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ (S.X.presheaf) (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat)
          (S.X.ringCatSheaf.property)⟩).obj
        ((Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField S.f))).obj (L))) 1) :=
  S.isZero_firstCohomology_dualizingSheafOverField_tensor L
    (S.nonempty_generatingSections_of_isRelativelyVeryAmple L hL).some
    (S.not_isTrivial_of_two_le_invertibleCurveDegree L hd)

end CohenMacaulayCurveSituation

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
